    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-10-29T13:35:59Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n'mini.base16' follows the [Base16 color scheme system](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16) with reference implementation being [chriskempson/base16-vim](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16-vim). So enabling any extra styling for bases is out of scope.\r\n\r\nThe suggested solution here is to manually override highlight groups that need tweaking with `vim.api.nvim_set_hl()` or `vim.cmd.highlight()`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.base16' follows the <a href=\"https://github.com/chriskempson/base16\">Base16 color scheme system</a> with reference implementation being <a href=\"https://github.com/chriskempson/base16-vim\">chriskempson/base16-vim</a>. So enabling any extra styling for bases is out of scope.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The suggested solution here is to manually override highlight groups that need tweaking with <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_set_hl()</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.cmd.highlight()</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n'mini.base16' follows the Base16 color scheme system with reference implementation being chriskempson/base16-vim. So enabling any extra styling for bases is out of scope.\nThe suggested solution here is to manually override highlight groups that need tweaking with vim.api.nvim_set_hl() or vim.cmd.highlight().",
